headers {
  Accept-Language: {{acceptLanguage}}
  X-Channel-Id: {{channelId}}
  X-Correlation-Id: {{$guid}}
  Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}
}

docs {
  Settings (both gateway addresses, login, page size, language, channel) live in the Local environment — select it before running.
  Change the gateway address or login there only.

  Every request sends Accept-Language, X-Channel-Id, and a fresh X-Correlation-Id and Idempotency-Key.
  The API ignores the key on /connect/* (login and token calls), so token responses are never stored.

  Run Accounts/Login first — it saves accessToken for the other requests.

  Values the scripts save (tokens, ids from Add requests) go into the Local environment as unsaved, in-memory
  values: you can see and edit them there, and a request's own Vars (pinned ids) override them.
}
